225. **Missing Rate-Limiting on Master PIN Verification**: Users can attempt infinite PIN entries against `verifyMasterPin` because lockout logic only applies to `verifyManagerPin`.
226. **Replay Attack on Audit Logs**: If an audit record is duplicated and injected with an identical hash, verification detects a duplicate but cannot determine which one is legitimate.
227. **Missing Hardware Security Module (HSM) / KeyStore Integration**: Master keys are derived via software PBKDF2 instead of leveraging Android Keystore (Tee/StrongBox).
228. **Staff Deactivation Takes Effect Only on Next Login**: If an active staff member is deactivated in Super Admin, their ongoing session is not invalidated until they manually log out.
229. **Unbounded Audit Log Growth**: Audit logs are never archived; after 100,000 transactions, Genesis hash verification traverses the entire chain sequentially, hanging the UI thread on load.
230. **Windowed Audit Verification Skips Intermediate Chain Blocks**: `verifyAuditChainWindowed` verifies only the last `windowSize` entries, failing to detect tampering that occurred prior to the window start.
